--- 3. re-calibrate on all days so far
# Calibration report (2026-09-28)

3967 rows, 367 tokens, 6 day(s) (2026-09-22 to 2026-09-28). Target: cost of selling immediately across all measured venues, vs consolidated mid. 5-fold CV grouped by token.
3305 more sales could not be absorbed by the merged book at all (no venue truncated). They can't be fitted, so they're scored instead: 'false comfort' = share a model prices under 10%. Dropped: 683 sales where a venue capped its levels (thin vs truncated unknowable); 0 token-days with no CMC volume/sigma.

| model | Y | delta | median abs err | median factor off | R^2 (log) | false comfort |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| textbook sqrt, global Y **(shipped)** | 1.66 | 0.500 | 14.1 bps | x1.81 | 0.484 | 81% |
| power law, global Y | 7.12 | 0.717 | 16.3 bps | x1.80 | 0.531 | 46% |
| learned Y per token | per token | 0.717 | 14.4 bps | x1.71 | 0.622 | 47% |

Median absolute error by order size (out-of-fold, bps):

| size | n | sqrt | power | learned |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| $10,000 | 1774 | 8.8 | 8.3 | 7.2 |
| $100,000 | 1571 | 25.2 | 33.5 | 28.3 |
| $1,000,000 | 502 | 24.0 | 36.6 | 34.4 |
| $10,000,000 | 120 | 91.7 | 85.6 | 91.6 |

What predicts a token's Y (GBM feature importance): log_sigma 0.48, history_days 0.19, turnover 0.13, log_mcap 0.12, log_volume 0.08

The learned model did not beat the power law by the required 5%, so the power law ships. Published as a negative result.

Wrote ingest/calibration.json (used by impact.py) and data/calibration_report.md (for METHODOLOGY.md).
